|\n|---|---|\n| *Lactobacillus bulgaricus* | Ferments lactose; produces lactic acid; transient gut coloniser |\n| *Streptococcus thermophilus* | Ferments lactose; produces lactic acid; supports mucosal immunity |\n\nSome brands (Siggi''s, Fage, Chobani) add additional probiotic strains (L. acidophilus, Bifidobacterium lactis). These strains are more likely to colonise the gut long-term. Check the label for \"live and active cultures\" seal.\n\n**Casey Means'' target: 3+ probiotic servings per day.** Greek yogurt as a breakfast or snack makes one of these servings practical and protein-rich."], "dosage_and_timing_guidance": "> [!info] Daily probiotic servings\n> **Optimal: 150\u2013200g per serving; 1\u20132 servings per day**\n>\n> Casey Means recommends 3+ servings of fermented foods daily. Greek yogurt can cover 1\u20132 of these if eaten at breakfast and as a snack; the remainder can come from kimchi, sauerkraut, or kefir.\n>\n> **Lactose intolerance:** the straining process and fermentation reduce lactose content to ~3.2g per 100g (vs. 4.8g in regular milk). Many people with mild lactose intolerance tolerate Greek yogurt well. Severely intolerant individuals should trial a small portion first.\n>\n> **Upper limit:** no meaningful upper limit for metabolically healthy individuals. Large amounts (400g+) in one sitting add significant saturated fat and calories \u2014 spread across the day is more effective than one large dose for microbiome diversity.\n\n---", "meal_ideas": "Plain with blueberries and chia seeds \u00b7 Layered with oats as overnight \"yogurt oats\" \u00b7 Post-training protein source \u00b7 As a base for dressings in place of mayonnaise\n\n**Pairs well with:** [[\ud83c\udf9b\ufe0f Control Center/Supabase Data/Foods/Blueberries]] \u00b7 [[\ud83c\udf9b\ufe0f Control Center/Supabase Data/Foods/Chia Seeds]] \u00b7 [[\ud83c\udf9b\ufe0f Control Center/Supabase Data/Foods/Oats]] \u00b7 [[\ud83c\udf9b\ufe0f Control Center/Supabase Data/Foods/Walnuts]]\n\n---", "good_energy_relevance": "The gut microbiome is the fourth root cause of metabolic dysfunction in the Good Energy framework (gut dysbiosis). Greek yogurt directly addresses this \u2014 the live cultures populate the gut, produce short-chain fatty acids (SCFAs), and improve the intestinal barrier that prevents endotoxins from triggering systemic inflammation. B12 supports mitochondrial energy production, and the low GI (11) means it causes almost no glucose perturbation.\n\n**Good Energy daily targets contribution (per 200g):**\n- Fibre: 0g of 50g target\n- Omega-3: 100mg of 2,000mg target\n- Antioxidants: low\n- Probiotics: \u2713 1 of 3 daily probiotic servings\n\n---"}'::jsonb) on conflict (name) do update set calories_per_100g = excluded.calories_per_100g, protein_per_100g = excluded.protein_per_100g, raw_payload = excluded.raw_payload;
insert into food_library (name, food_category, calories_per_100g, protein_per_100g, carbs_per_100g, fat_per_100g, fibre_per_100g, omega3_per_100g_mg, seed_oil, raw_payload) values ('Hazelnuts', 'fat', 190, 4, 5, 18, 0, 0, false, '{"content_hash": "a719b4d4273da7c6a41990b0a8a661a0", "full_markdown_content": "---\ntags:\n  - nutrition/food\n  - nutrition/food/fat\nfood_category: fat\nsource: notion\nnotion_category: Fat\nserving_unit: \"1/4 cup (30g)\"\nserving_unit_g: 30\ncalories_per_unit: 190\nprotein_per_unit_g: 4\ncarbs_per_unit_g: 5\nfat_per_unit_g: 18\nfiber_per_unit_g: 3\nsugar_per_unit_g: 1\nprocessing_level: \"Whole/Unprocessed\"\nfermented: false\n---\n# Hazelnuts\n\nMigrated from Notion''s Foods database. Data is per serving **unit**, not per 100g \u2014 a sparser reference than the vault''s primary food-library entries.\n\n## Macros (per unit)\n\n| Unit | Calories | Protein | Carbs | Sugar | Fat | Fiber |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1/4 cup (30g) | 190 | 4g | 5g | 1g | 18g | 3g |\n\n## Micronutrients (per unit)\n\n| Nutrient | Amount |\n|---|---|\n| Calcium | 30mg |\n| Iron | 1.5mg |\n| Potassium | 200mg |\n| Sodium | 0mg |\n\n## Classification\n\n- **Category:** Fat\n- **Processing Level:** Whole/Unprocessed\n- **Fermented:** No\n", "portion_state": "unspecified", "tables": [{"headers": ["Unit", "Calories", "Protein", "Carbs", "Sugar", "Fat", "Fiber"], "rows": [{"Unit": "1/4 cup (30g)", "Calories": "190", "Protein": "4g", "Carbs": "5g", "Sugar": "1g", "Fat": "18g", "Fiber": "3g"}]}, {"headers": ["Nutrient", "Amount"], "rows": [{"Nutrient": "Calcium", "Amount": "30mg"}, {"Nutrient": "Iron", "Amount": "1.5mg"}, {"Nutrient": "Potassium", "Amount": "200mg"}, {"Nutrient": "Sodium", "Amount": "0mg"}]}], "unit": "1/4 cup (30g)", "calories": "190", "protein": "4g", "carbs": "5g", "sugar": "1g", "fat": "18g", "fiber": "3g", "quick_reference_servings": [{"Nutrient": "Calcium", "Amount": "30mg"}, {"Nutrient": "Iron", "Amount": "1.5mg"}, {"Nutrient": "Potassium", "Amount": "200mg"}, {"Nutrient": "Sodium", "Amount": "0mg"}], "tags": "", "food_category": "fat", "source": "notion", "notion_category": "Fat", "serving_unit": "1/4 cup (30g)", "serving_unit_g": "30", "calories_per_unit": "190", "protein_per_unit_g": "4", "carbs_per_unit_g": "5", "fat_per_unit_g": "18", "fiber_per_unit_g": "3", "sugar_per_unit_g": "1", "processing_level": "Whole/Unprocessed", "fermented": "false", "callouts": [], "quotes": []}'::jsonb) on conflict (name) do update set calories_per_100g = excluded.calories_per_100g, protein_per_100g = excluded.protein_per_100g, raw_payload = excluded.raw_payload;
