"\"Variety in polyphenol sources is not a minor detail \u2014 different anthocyanins activate different antioxidant pathways. A mix of berries covers more biological ground than the same dose of one berry.\" \u2014 Rhonda Patrick", "content": ""}, {"type": "info", "title": "Frozen = nutritionally equivalent or superior", "content": "Frozen at peak ripeness, this blend typically retains more anthocyanins and vitamin C than out-of-season fresh berries. The frozen format also makes it a consistent year-round source regardless of seasonal availability."}, {"type": "warning", "title": "Verify current label", "content": "Exact macros vary slightly between production batches and packaging runs. The values here reflect the typical nutritional profile \u2014 always cross-check against the current Costco package label, particularly for fibre and sugar."}, {"type": "tip", "title": "Why the blend outperforms a single berry", "content": "Each berry contributes distinct polyphenol classes that activate different biological pathways. Eating the three together provides broader coverage than a larger serving of any one berry."}, {"type": "info", "title": "Same practical range as pure blueberries", "content": "**Optimal: 80\u2013150g per day**\n- 80g delivers ~2.8g fibre, ~14mg vitamin C, and a meaningful polyphenol dose\n- 120\u2013150g is appropriate when the blend is the primary fruit source for the day\n\n**Frozen from frozen:** no need to thaw before eating \u2014 frozen berries can be added directly to oats, yogurt, or a smoothie. Thawed berries soften quickly; use promptly after thawing.\n\n**No upper limit concern** for metabolically healthy individuals. Natural sugars (7.5g/100g) are well-buffered by fibre and the anti-glycaemic effects of the polyphenols."}], "quotes": ["\"Variety in polyphenol sources is not a minor detail \u2014 different anthocyanins activate different antioxidant pathways. A mix of berries covers more biological ground than the same dose of one berry.\"